<% content_for :title, "The science behind Kept" %>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:860px">
  <span class="eyebrow">The science</span><h1>What Kept is built on</h1>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Dosing</h3><p class="muted">Dose ladders, step intervals and missed-dose windows come from each medicine’s prescribing information (e.g. tirzepatide weekly in 2.5 mg steps every 4 weeks, missed doses within 4 days; semaglutide 0.25→2.4 mg; the Wegovy pill 1.5→25 mg daily on an empty stomach; Foundayo once daily without food restrictions). Kept never changes a dose — it tells you what the label says and when to ask.</p>
    <h3>Protein & muscle</h3><p class="muted">Targets follow a 2025 joint advisory of four professional societies: 1.2–1.6 g of protein per kg per day during active GLP-1 weight loss, with adjusted body weight above BMI 30, and structured resistance training at least three times a week. Trials report lean mass at roughly a quarter (tirzepatide) to over a third (semaglutide) of weight lost without specific intervention; Kept’s estimate scales those baselines by your protein and training adherence.</p>
    <h3>Persistence and regain</h3><p class="muted">In a 2025 cohort of 125,474 adults, 64.8% of those without diabetes stopped within 12 months. A 2026 meta-analysis of 48 studies estimated about 60% of lost weight returns within a year of stopping; a Cleveland Clinic real-world study found 45% kept the weight off at one year, many by restarting or switching treatment. Kept treats stopping as a planned transition.</p>
    <h3>Weight trend</h3><p class="muted">An exponential moving average (α = 0.1) smooths daily water swings. Kept flags loss faster than 1.5% a week (more lean-mass loss), a flat trend for a month after 12 weeks (plateau) and a 2% rise over four weeks (regain).</p>
    <h3>Safety</h3><p class="muted">Red flags mirror label warnings: pancreatitis, gallbladder disease, dehydration and acute kidney injury, hypoglycaemia with insulin or sulfonylureas, and hypersensitivity reactions.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>
